# Build output. `main.js` is the esbuild bundle, produced by `make build`; the
# release workflow attaches it to the GitHub release. The leading slashes anchor
# these to the repository root so they cannot match anything inside the vendored
# numbat checkout.
#
# `src/wasm/pkg` is deliberately NOT here, though it is generated too. Building
# it needs a Rust toolchain, a matching wasm-bindgen and binaryen, none of which
# a plain `npm ci && npm run build` has — and that build is what Obsidian's
# plugin review runs. Committing the bindings is what lets a clean checkout
# produce a bundle. `make wasm` regenerates them when NUMBAT_TAG moves; the
# release workflow rebuilds them from pinned source regardless, so what ships is
# never merely what was committed here.
/main.js
/main.js.map

# The pinned sharkdp/numbat checkout and its cargo target directory.
/.build/

# npm
/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Nix build results
/result
/result-*

# Obsidian plugin data, present when the repository is symlinked into a vault
# for testing.
/data.json

# The local development runbook: session state and working notes, not user
# documentation.
/PLAN.md

# Editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.idea/
/.vscode/
